# Findings trivy config (ci.yml's trivy-config job) accepts, with why. Each
# is something hyve needs to do its job, not a mistake to fix; see the
# comments on each rule in deploy/helm/hyve/templates/controller-rbac.yaml.

# The controller's ClusterRole reads Secrets (whether a resource's Secrets
# exist) and creates them (push delivery's Job inputs and packaged charts,
# in the child cluster's namespace). It can't list, update or delete them
# cluster-wide.
KSV-0041

# The controller's ClusterRole can get and update its own two webhook
# configurations (by resourceNames): it makes its webhook certificate at
# start-up and sets the CA on them.
KSV-0114

# With the host enabled (the second chart scan):
# hyve-cluster-owner is a role template, after Rancher's Cluster Owner: its
# rules are written to child clusters for ClusterAccess, and it's never
# bound on the management cluster (templates/access-roles.yaml).
KSV-0044
KSV-0046

# The host execs into the kubectl shell's pods, only in the hyve-shell
# namespace (internal/shell).
KSV-0053
